# DMGKINDS - damage kinds and monster vulnerabilities for Begotten.
#
# Every weapon attack deals a damage KIND, and every kind belongs to a CATEGORY:
#
#   kinds:       blade  bullet shell belt   fire tempest spirit   hellfire
#   categories:  melee  [------ firearm ---] [------ magic -----]  special
#
# Lines (anything after # or // is a comment, "=" and "," are ignored):
#
#   weapon <name|number> <kind>
#       the kind dealt by the weapon in the player's hands (hitscan and melee).
#       names: fist pistol shotgun chaingun missile plasma bfg chainsaw supershotgun
#              dualpistols chainfire tornado arclightning snap hellfire spare
#       (modes: knife=fist, pistol=pistol, revolver=dualpistols, rifle=shotgun, machinegun=chaingun,
#        fireball=missile, devil's breath=plasma, thunderclap=bfg, scattergun=supershotgun,
#        chaingun=chainfire)
#
#   projectile thing <N> <kind>      (or: projectile ednum <N> <kind>)
#   projectile name <tornado|arcbolt|hellfire> <kind>    (Begotten's own projectiles)
#       the kind dealt by a projectile, and by its explosion. N is the DEHACKED
#       thing number (1 = player, 34 = rocket, 35 = plasma, 36 = BFG ball).
#
#   vulnerability thing <N> <kind-or-category> <percent> [<...> <percent>]...
#   vulnerability ednum <N> ...      (ednum = the number used in the map editor)
#       how much damage this monster takes, in percent (100 = normal, 0 = immune).
#       A kind overrides its category; anything not listed is 100%.
#       Later lines (and later DMGKINDS lumps in your own WAD) override earlier ones.
#

weapon fist         blade
weapon chainsaw     blade
weapon pistol       bullet     # revolver
weapon dualpistols  bullet
weapon shotgun      shell      # rifle
weapon supershotgun shell      # scattergun
weapon chaingun     belt       # machinegun
weapon chainfire    belt       # chaingun
weapon missile      fire       # fireball
weapon plasma       fire       # devil's breath
weapon tornado      tempest
weapon arclightning tempest
weapon snap         spirit
weapon bfg          spirit     # thunderclap
weapon hellfire     hellfire
weapon spare        hellfire

projectile thing 34 fire      # rocket
projectile thing 35 fire      # plasma ball
projectile thing 36 spirit    # BFG ball (and its tracers)
projectile thing 43 spirit    # BFG spray
projectile name tornado  tempest
projectile name arcbolt  tempest
projectile name hellfire hellfire

# The roster took over Doom's monsters (same editor numbers), so the numbers below are Doom's.
# Starting values to be playtested; edit freely.
#
# Modern (humans): weak to bullets/shells, a bit resistant to magic.
vulnerability ednum 3004 firearm 115 magic 80      # pistol trooper
vulnerability ednum 9    firearm 115 magic 80      # shotgun trooper
vulnerability ednum 84   firearm 115 magic 80      # SMG trooper
vulnerability ednum 65   firearm 115 magic 80      # chaingun trooper
vulnerability ednum 21001 firearm 115 magic 80     # rocket trooper (new number)
vulnerability ednum 68   firearm 115 magic 80      # shock trooper
# Medieval: weak to magic.
vulnerability ednum 3002 magic 125 firearm 90      # werewolf
vulnerability ednum 3001 magic 125 firearm 90      # fire elemental
vulnerability ednum 66   magic 125 firearm 90      # mad wizard
vulnerability ednum 69   magic 125 firearm 90      # apprentice
vulnerability ednum 3003 magic 125 firearm 90      # minister
vulnerability ednum 67   firearm 35 magic 150      # golem: stone
# Alien (mindeater 64, aegis 58, bore 3005, conjurer 71, hatred 3006): no particular vulnerabilities.
# Bosses
vulnerability ednum 16   firearm 50                # mecha: armoured
vulnerability ednum 7    magic 40                  # giant beetle: resists magic
